{"authors": [], "discovered_at": "2026-11-06T03:20:50.260385Z", "id": "github:release:535360445:release:435618761", "kind": "release", "matched_terms": [], "metadata": {"action": "released", "draft": false, "forks": 11970, "prerelease": false, "stars": 63169, "stars_delta": 35, "tag_name": "v8.4.203"}, "organization": "ultralytics", "priority": {"source": 0.5}, "published_at": "2026-11-05T19:12:31Z", "related_items": [], "scores": {}, "source": "github", "source_id": "535360445:release:435618761", "summary": "## \ud83c\udf1f Summary\n**v8.4.203** adds NXP i.MX95 Neutron NPU export for YOLO models, plus security improvements and fixes across training, inference, tracking, and visualization.\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Key Changes\n- \ud83d\ude80 **NXP i.MX95 export:** Export with `format=nxp` to create an INT8 LiteRT model compiled using Neutron SDK 3.3.0. The export supports all seven YOLO tasks and uses the existing LiteRT inference backend with NXP\u2019s delegate. It targets **i.MX95 only**; unsupported operations may run on the CPU.\n- \ud83d\udd12 **Safer loading:** Dataset caches now use a restricted unpickler. Checkpoints no longer trigger automatic package installation, and SAM, NAS, YOLO-World, and YOLOE loading paths use safer weights-only loading where supported.\n- \ud83e\udde0 **Training fixes:** YOLOE text-prompt training now handles smaller class counts correctly, hand-keypoint flips preserve landmark assignments, and deterministic semantic-segmentation loss computation is faster.\n- \ud83c\udfaf **Inference and tracking fixes:** Tracker assignment now finds better matches in the SciPy fallback. FastSAM box prompts that miss all masks select none, and SAM prompts remain usable after an interrupted \u201csegment everything\u201d call.\n- \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f **Utility improvements:** Fixed mask-IoU behavior across data types, backend precision updates after model conversions, ExecuTorch capture issues, binary semantic-mask rendering, and PIL text placement.\n- \ud83d\udcda **Dataset workflow updates:** Argoverse now downloads and converts through Ultralytics Platform instead of Google Drive. Documentation also clarifies how dataset subsets are selected and adds NXP to the listed export options.\n\n## \ud83c\udfaf Purpose & Impact\n- NXP i.MX95 users can compile YOLO models for Neutron hardware using the existing export and inference workflows. Validate accuracy, latency, and CPU fallback on the target board before deployment.\n- Safer loading reduces risks from untrusted cache and model files; missing checkpoint dependencies now raise an error rather than being installed automatically.\n- The reliability fixes address issues that could cause incorrect matches, unexpected masks, training failures, or plotting errors.\n- Faster deterministic semantic-loss computation can reduce training overhead, though the reported speedups are focused measurements rather than guarantees of end-to-end training speed.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Fix suboptimal matches in tracker assignment fallback and skip unused lap cost by @Y-T-G in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27026\n* Runner CPU image: Chromium system libraries for Playwright screenshots by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27030\n* Remove Google Drive downloads and use Platform for Argoverse by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27033\n* Use weights only loading for SAM and NAS checkpoints by @Y-T-G in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27032\n* Check for sudo with shutil.which instead of a shell call by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27034\n* Map hand-keypoints flip_idx to identity so flipped hands keep their landmarks by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27024\n* Stop auto-installing packages named by untrusted checkpoints by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27035\n* Clarify fraction subset selection for image-folder datasets by @JaypeeLan in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27029\n* Remove duplicate Platform training command serialization by @laodouya in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27004\n* Plot only the foreground of binary semantic masks by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27025\n* Speed up semantic segmentation training 2.8x under deterministic mode by @Y-T-G in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27027\n* Accept tuple coordinates in `Annotator.text` with PIL fonts by @MohammadHijjawi97 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27038\n* Load dataset cache files with a restricted unpickler by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27041\n* Select nothing for FastSAM box prompts that overlap no mask by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27043\n* Keep SAM prompts working after an interrupted segment-everything call by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27046\n* Promote non-float masks to float32 in mask_iou by @cainiao33 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27039\n* Synchronize backend precision after module conversions by @aswanth-07 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27040\n* Capture ExecuTorch exports on CPU to fix wrong MPS output and CUDA crashes by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27044\n* Load YOLO-World and YOLOE text embedding caches with weights_only by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27045\n* Fix YOLOE prompt losses and CPU runner image builds by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27048\n* Add NXP i.MX95 Neutron export by @glenn-jocher in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27047\n\n## New Contributors\n* @JaypeeLan made their first contribution in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/27029\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.202...v8.4.203\n", "title": "ultralytics/ultralytics v8.4.203 - Add NXP i.MX95 Neutron export (#27047)", "topics": ["image_classification", "instance_segmentation", "object_detection", "object_tracking", "semantic_segmentation"], "updated_at": "2026-11-05T19:14:15Z", "url": "https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/tag/v8.4.203", "venue": null}
